<article class="env-lemma" id="05SM">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05SM">Lemma <span data-tag="05SM">12.19.10</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. Let $A, B, C \in \text{Fil}(\mathcal{A})$. Let $f : A \to B$ and $g : A \to C$ be morphisms. Then there exists a pushout </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ A \ar[r]_ f \ar[d]_ g &  B \ar[d]^{g'} \\  C \ar[r]^{f'} &  C \amalg _ A B }  \]
</div>
  <p> in $\text{Fil}(\mathcal{A})$. If $f$ is strict, so is $f'$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Set $C \amalg _ A B$ equal to $\mathop{\mathrm{Coker}}((g, -f) : A \to C \oplus B)$ in $\text{Fil}(\mathcal{A})$. This cokernel exists, by Lemma <a href="/tag/0122" data-tag="0122">12.19.2</a>. It is a pushout, see Example <a href="/tag/05PJ" data-tag="05PJ">12.5.6</a>. Note that $F^ p(C \amalg _ A B)$ is the image of $F^ pC \oplus F^ pB$. Hence 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  (f')^{-1}(F^ p(C \amalg _ A B)) = g(f^{-1}(F^ pB)) + F^ pC  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Whence the last statement. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>